.\" Made from the kstar help (src/help.rs); do not edit. See src/manual.rs.
.TH KSTAR-EXPORT 1 "" "Kleene Star" "Kleene Star Manual"
.SH NAME
kstar\-export \- write machine M as Rust, Python or JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBkstar export\fR [options] <file> <machine>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Runs the file without showing its output, then writes <machine> to a file
next to <file>, named after the machine (HasDouble1.rs, HasDouble1.py or
HasDouble1.json), and says where:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Wrote C:\eUsers\eme\eHasDouble1.rs (Rust, 42 lines)
.fi
.RE
.PP
It never replaces a file that is already there unless given \-\-force.
.PP
As Rust (the default), the file is one dependency-free function
\fBpub fn name(input: &str) -> bool\fR that accepts exactly the machine's
words, with a \fB#[cfg(test)]\fR module of sample words. As Python, it is one
dependency-free file with \fBdef name(word: str) -> bool\fR that checks itself
on sample words when run as a script. For both, <machine> may be any
regular language (Dfa, Nfa, Regex or Set[Str]), such as \fBEvenZeros\fR or
\fBto_dfa(r)\fR; it is turned into a DFA first.
.PP
As JSON it writes <machine> in Kleene Star's JSON format, which \fBfrom_json\fR
reads back: any Dfa, Nfa, Regex, Grammar, Pda or Tm, kept as it is, with
its state names.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
rust (the default), python or json
.TP
\fB\-\-fn\fR \fI<name>\fR
the function's name (default: <machine> in snake_case); not with \-\-format json
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fI<path>\fR
write to this file, or into this folder; \fB\-o \-\fR prints to standard output instead of writing a file
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
replace the file if it is already there
.TP
\fB\-\-minimize\fR
minimize the DFA first, for the smallest table
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<when>\fR
auto (the default), always or never. With auto, output is coloured only on a terminal and never when the NO_COLOR environment variable is set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBkstar export examples/01_dfa.kstar HasDouble1\fR
write HasDouble1.rs next to the file
.TP
\fBkstar export \-\-format python lab.kstar M \-o \-\fR
print M as a Python function
.TP
\fBkstar export \-\-format json lab.kstar G \-o out/ \-\-force\fR
write out/G.json, replacing it
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkstar\fR(1),
\fBkstar\-help\fR(1)
.PP
The reference and the tutorial: https://github.com/Pratham71/kleene\-star
